{
  "title": "Chain of Thought Empowers Transformers to Solve Inherently Serial Problems",
  "authors": [
    "Zhiyuan Li",
    "Hong Liu",
    "Denny Zhou",
    "Tengyu Ma"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "arxivId": "2402.12875",
  "abstract": "This paper explores how instructing large language models to generate a sequence of intermediate steps, or a chain of thought, can improve their accuracy on arithmetic and symbolic reasoning tasks. The authors provide a theoretical understanding of the power of chain of thought for decoder-only transformers and demonstrate its effectiveness in solving inherently serial problems.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The core idea is to instruct large language models to generate a sequence of intermediate steps, or a chain of thought, to improve their accuracy on arithmetic and symbolic reasoning tasks. This approach allows the model to perform inherently serial computations, which are otherwise lacking in transformers, especially when depth is low. <strong>Chain of thought</strong> enables the model to solve complex problems that require serial computations.",
