    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The authors define a complexity class, CoT, which consists of problems solvable by a transformer with a constant depth, constant precision, and T steps of chain of thought. They show that constant-depth transformers with CoT can solve problems that are not solvable by constant-depth transformers without CoT. The <strong>chain of thought</strong> is constructed to simulate the values of each gate in the increasing order of id, allowing the transformer to compute the value of the current gate using attention and a feedforward network.",
