    {
      "title": "The Results",
      "content": "The authors demonstrate the effectiveness of chain of thought in solving inherently serial problems, such as permutation composition, iterated squaring, and circuit value problem. They show that transformers with chain of thought outperform those without chain of thought, especially when the depth is small. The <strong>experimental results</strong> support the theoretical analysis, highlighting the importance of chain of thought in improving the expressiveness of transformers.",
